      "text": "Let the two integers be \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). We are given that the least common multiple (LCM) of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is 36 and their greatest common divisor (GCD) is 6. We need to find the product of the two numbers, \\(a \\times b\\).\n\nThe relationship between the LCM and GCD of two numbers is given by the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(a, b) \\times \\text{GCD}(a, b) = a \\times b\n\\]\nSubstituting the given values into the formula, we get:\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = a \\times b\n\\]\nSimplifying the left side, we have:\n\\[\n216 = a \\times b\n\\]\nThus, the product of the two numbers is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{216}\n\\]",
